file=Legal & Compliance/comply/operational/agent/comply-config.md · h=agent: comply\ndepartment: Legal & Compliance\ntype: config\npurpose: >\nWatchlist, materiality tiers, feed configuration, jurisdictions, regimes catalog,\nescalation matrix, review cadence, and house style. Read by reg-monitor-routing\nto bind YVON's config layer to the reg-feed-watcher marketplace skill. Read by\nobligation-register and regulated-activity-readiness for jurisdiction/regime scope.\nField list derived from actual skill references — every field traces to a line in\none of comply's SKILL.md files.\nrequired_by:\n- custom/reg-monitor-routing/SKILL.md   # Step 2 checks these sections by name\n- custom/obligation-register/SKILL.md   # jurisdiction + escalation matrix\n- custom/regulated-activity-readiness/SKILL.md   # regimes catalog + escalation\n- marketplace/reg-feed-watcher/SKILL.md   # via the wrapper\nconfig_debt_announcement: >\nEvery <FILL_IN> in this file is a config debt announced on every skill\ninvocation (playbook §14.7). Fill the value or mark it `n/a` with a one-line\nreason.\nlast_updated: 2026-07-29\n · c·c:comply \· config=> **HOW TO USE.** Fill each `<FILL_IN>` with a real value or replace with `n/a — <one-line reason>`. Section headings are contract with `reg-monitor-routing`, `obligation-register`, and `regulated-activity-readiness` — do not rename.\n\n · tb=\| Field \| Value \| · tb=\|---\|---\| · tb=\| Role of the operator \| `<FILL_IN — lawyer / paralegal / compliance officer / non-lawyer>` \| · tb=\| Contact for compliance escalations \| `<FILL_IN — name or role>` \| · tb=\| DPO / Privacy officer (if applicable) \| `<FILL_IN>` \| · tb=\| Jurisdiction code \| Notes \| · tb=\|---\|---\| · tb=\| `<FILL_IN — e.g., US-federal>` \| `<FILL_IN>` \| · tb=\| `<FILL_IN — e.g., US-CA>` \| `<FILL_IN>` \| · tb=\| `<FILL_IN — e.g., EU>` \| `<FILL_IN>` \| · jis:Jurisdictions in scope=No hardcoded jurisdiction (playbook §0.4b). Add or remove rows freely.\n\n · w:Watchlist=Regulators to monitor via `reg-feed-watcher`. At least one required for feed checks to run.\n · tb=\| Regulator \| Source type \| Slug / URL \| Notes \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| `<FILL_IN — e.g., FTC>` \| `federal-register-slug` \| `federal-trade-commission` \| `<FILL_IN>` \| · tb=\| `<FILL_IN>` \| `rss` \| `<FILL_IN URL>` \| `<FILL_IN>` \| · tb=\| `<FILL_IN>` \| `paid-mcp` \| `<FILL_IN identifier>` \| `<FILL_IN — only if MCP configured>` \| · mt:Materiality tiers=Definitions used by `reg-feed-watcher` Step 2 to classify feed items.\n · tb=\| Tier \| Definition \| · tb=\|---\|---\| · tb=\| 🔴 Always material \| `<FILL_IN — e.g., "final rule from watchlist regulator that touches our sectors">` \| · tb=\| 🟡 Review-worthy \| `<FILL_IN>` \| · tb=\| 📝 FYI \| `<FILL_IN>` \| · tb=\| skip \| `<FILL_IN — what gets filtered out>` \| · fc:Feed configuration=Aggregate of Tier 1 (free), Tier 2 (paid MCP), and Tier 3 (manual) sources.\n · tb=\| Tier \| Enabled \| Notes \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| Tier 1 — Federal Register API + direct RSS \| ✅ default \| Free; requires web fetch permission \| · tb=\| Tier 2 — Paid regulatory feed MCP \| `<FILL_IN — yes/no; if yes, MCP name>` \| Requires MCP connected \| · tb=\| Tier 2 — CourtListener MCP \| `<FILL_IN — yes/no>` \| Requires MCP connected \| · tb=\| Tier 3 — Manual entry \| ✅ always available \| No config needed \| · fc:Feed configuration=Digest output path: `<FILL_IN — e.g., "~/regulatory-legal-digests/reg-digest-YYYY-MM-DD.md" or "chat only">`.\n\n · tb=\| Field \| Value \| · tb=\|---\|---\| · tb=\| Enabled \| `<FILL_IN — yes/no>` \| · tb=\| Default owner for comment decisions \| `<FILL_IN — role or name>` \| · tb=\| Comment tracker file path \| `<FILL_IN — default: ~/.claude/plugins/config/…/comment-tracker.yaml>` \| · rc:Regimes catalog=For each (category × jurisdiction) tuple, which regime applies. Used by `regulated-activity-readiness` Step 3.\n · tb=\| Category \| Jurisdiction \| Regime \| Compliance path (default) \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| `<FILL_IN — e.g., money-services>` \| `<FILL_IN — e.g., US-federal>` \| `<FILL_IN — e.g., BSA/AML + FinCEN MSB>` \| `<FILL_IN>` \| · tb=\| `<FILL_IN>` \| `<FILL_IN>` \| `<FILL_IN>` \| `<FILL_IN>` \| · rc:Regimes catalog=Add rows as the operator declares new jurisdictions or categories. Never invent regimes (playbook §0.5).\n\n · ac:Always-L3 categories=Categories that auto-escalate to `Governance/board` on any BLOCKED or UNKNOWN verdict from `regulated-activity-readiness`, regardless of launch date:\n\n- money-services / payments / money-transmitter\n- deposit-taking / banking\n- investment / broker-dealer / securities\n- health-data / PHI\n- credit-reporting\n\n`<FILL_IN — add or remove categories per your risk posture>`\n\n · em:Escalation matrix=Feed check + register + readiness all share this ladder. Approver names must be real; L3 is fixed to `Governance/board`.\n · tb=\| Level \| Threshold \| Approver \| Notes \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| L1 \| Feed item = FYI \· Register update = routine attestation \· Readiness = CLEAR \| comply itself \| No external sign-off \| · tb=\| L2 \| Feed item = review-worthy \· Register update = new obligation or scope change \· Readiness = CONDITIONAL \| `<FILL_IN — role or named person>` \| Business-unit / GC review \| · tb=\| L3 \| Feed item = always-material \· Register attestation > 20% overdue \· Readiness = BLOCKED \· any always-L3 category \| `Governance/board` \| Fixed — constitutional threshold \| · tb=\| Field \| Value \| · tb=\|---\|---\| · tb=\| Obligation register review cadence \| `<FILL_IN — quarterly by default; can be monthly or annual>` \| · tb=\| Regulator-feed check cadence \| `<FILL_IN — daily / weekly / on-demand>` \| · tb=\| Regime catalog re-verification \| `<FILL_IN — annual>` \| · tb=\| Field \| Value \| · tb=\|---\|---\| · tb=\| Work-product header (default) \| `<FILL_IN — e.g., "PRIVILEGED AND CONFIDENTIAL — ATTORNEY WORK PRODUCT">` \| · tb=\| Privilege circle (default distribution) \| `<FILL_IN>` \| · tb=\| Preferred date format \| `<FILL_IN — e.g., "YYYY-MM-DD">` \| · tb=\| Preferred citation style \| `<FILL_IN — e.g., "Bluebook", "OSCOLA", or "n/a">` \| · tb=\| Digest format default \| `<FILL_IN — full-memo / slack-summary / both>` \| · tb=\| Section \| Fields \| Status \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| Who's using this \| 3 \| `<FILL_IN counter>` \| · tb=\| Jurisdictions in scope \| ≥1 required \| `<FILL_IN counter>` \| · tb=\| Watchlist \| ≥1 required \| `<FILL_IN counter>` \| · tb=\| Materiality tiers \| 4 \| `<FILL_IN counter>` \| · tb=\| Feed configuration \| 4 rows + digest path \| `<FILL_IN counter>` \| · tb=\| Comment tracker \| 3 \| `<FILL_IN counter>` \| · tb=\| Regimes catalog \| ≥1 row required per active jurisdiction \| `<FILL_IN counter>` \| · tb=\| Always-L3 categories \| 5 default + additions \| `<FILL_IN counter>` \| · tb=\| Escalation matrix \| 2 approver names (L1 fixed, L3 fixed) \| `<FILL_IN counter>` \| · tb=\| Review cadence \| 3 \| `<FILL_IN counter>` \| · tb=\| House style \| 5 \| `<FILL_IN counter>` \| · cds:Config debt summary=Any `<FILL_IN>` remaining is announced on every invocation per playbook §14.7.\n